{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1479818-was-it-ever-explained-why-dzurmath-could-go-over-6-in-his-write-up","id":1479818,"title":"Was it ever explained why Dzurmath could go over 6+ in his write up?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-30T10:23:27-07:00","id":1479818,"title":"Was it ever explained why Dzurmath could go over 6+ in his write up?","content":"I'm a really big fan of this game and one of things that bothered me in Grim Fears is that we had a True Fae character that didn't have the same 6 dot limit cap on his skills and attributes. Was this ever really explained at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T14:25:54-07:00","id":1479836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1479818-was-it-ever-explained-why-dzurmath-could-go-over-6-in-his-write-up#post1479818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a really big fan of this game and one of things that bothered me in Grim Fears is that we had a True Fae character that didn't have the same 6 dot limit cap on his skills and attributes. Was this ever really explained at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>He has a Fae Aspect that specifically exempts him from it. Possibly the narrative justification is something to do with the hunk of iron that's slowly killing him, but the mechanical reason is that he's a Legendary Monster who isn't subject to the cap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T20:43:46-07:00","id":1479857,"title":"","content":"In universe it isn't explained per say, but as Satchel said it is specifically noted that he isn't subject to the normal rules. As with a lot of the material the reason and the exact details are left up to the story teller to determine for their chronicle, and that's intentional to the toolkit approach. Weird exceptions invite you to ask why, and hopefully come up with interesting answers.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's a bargain he's learned during his centuries of research<br /> <br /> Maybe it's an unknown property of iron, and any True Fae in contact with it for long enough has their full potential unleashed, it's just that none of them would ever intentionally endure that kind of pain<br /> <br /> Maybe he traded away some other advantage long ago for it<br /> <br /> Maybe it's a specific property of one of his Titles that could be transferred to any other Fae<br /> <br /> The Doylist reason is of course that he exists to provide a challenge to exceptionally powerful Changelings. Sometimes normal True Fae just aren't scary enough","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T13:58:15-07:00","id":1480204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1479818-was-it-ever-explained-why-dzurmath-could-go-over-6-in-his-write-up?p=1479857#post1479857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In universe it isn't explained per say, but as Satchel said it is specifically noted that he isn't subject to the normal rules. As with a lot of the material the reason and the exact details are left up to the story teller to determine for their chronicle, and that's intentional to the toolkit approach. Weird exceptions invite you to ask why, and hopefully come up with interesting answers.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's a bargain he's learned during his centuries of research<br /> <br /> Maybe it's an unknown property of iron, and any True Fae in contact with it for long enough has their full potential unleashed, it's just that none of them would ever intentionally endure that kind of pain<br /> <br /> Maybe he traded away some other advantage long ago for it<br /> <br /> Maybe it's a specific property of one of his Titles that could be transferred to any other Fae<br /> <br /> The Doylist reason is of course that he exists to provide a challenge to exceptionally powerful Changelings. Sometimes normal True Fae just aren't scary enough</div> </div> </div> </div>That in itself is scary. When you consider that even in our plane of existence they have a big advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T16:07:59-07:00","id":1481623,"title":"","content":"I'd say it's because he's a freaking dragon, of course he's going to be one heck of a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}